<metadata>

  <!--
    Binding transforms that only apply from .NET 11 (android 37) onwards. Scoped by an explicit
    TransformFile Remove in Sentry.Bindings.Android.csproj, because the Android SDK auto-globs
    Transforms/**/*.xml into every TFM and an entry that matches nothing warns with BG8A00.
  -->

  <!--
    TombstoneParser.parse(Tombstone) takes com.abovevacant.epitaph.core.Tombstone, from the epitaph
    library that sentry-android-core depends on. We reference epitaph with Bind="false" (see the
    AndroidMavenLibrary items in Sentry.Bindings.Android.csproj), so there is no C# type for it, and
    the generated binding emits an unresolvable `global::Com.Abovevacant.Epitaph.Core.Tombstone`:

      error CS0400: The type or namespace name 'Com' could not be found in the global namespace

    The android 36 generator drops methods whose parameter types are unbound before the transforms
    run (the overload is in api.xml.class-parse but not api.xml), so this is unnecessary - and would
    warn BG8A00 - there. The android 37 generator keeps it, which is why this file exists.

    We never call TombstoneParser from C#, and the parameterless parse() overload is unaffected, so
    drop just the overload.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.sentry.android.core.internal.tombstone']/class[@name='TombstoneParser']/method[@name='parse' and count(parameter)=1 and parameter[1][@type='com.abovevacant.epitaph.core.Tombstone']]" />

</metadata>
